From 114c34c45ebac0adc1cbe2a0a4e4ab87528550a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:16:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] service: bind every connection of a message to the bearer
 interface

soupmessage_network_event_cb() binds the socket to the MMS bearer on
G_SOCKET_CLIENT_CONNECTING and then disconnects itself, so only the
first connection a message opens is bound. Any later one - libsoup
following a redirect, or GSocketClient moving on to the next address of
a host name - goes out unbound, over whatever the default route is.

Keep the handler connected for the life of the message. Also report a
failed bind as a warning with the reason instead of a debug line with
setsockopt()'s -1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/service.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/service.c b/src/service.c
index 24c35cb..738052a 100644
--- a/src/service.c
+++ b/src/service.c
@@ -3786,10 +3786,14 @@ soupmessage_network_event_cb (SoupMessage       *msg,
       if (return_code == 0)
         DBG ("Socket is bound to %s", request->service->interface);
       else
-        DBG ("Socket could not be bound! Error: %d", return_code);
+        g_warning ("Could not bind socket to %s: %s",
+                   request->service->interface, g_strerror (errno));
 
-      g_signal_handler_disconnect (msg,
-                                   request->soupmessage_network_event_signal_id);
+      /*
+       * Stay connected: a message can open more than one connection
+       * (another address of the host, a redirect), and each of them
+       * has to go out on the MMS bearer too.
+       */
     }
 }
 
